## 5. SCENE CONTRACT & REGISTRY

Every demo is an IIFE registering into a global: `window.DEMOS = {}` (line 2783), then `window.DEMOS[N] = { init, scene, staticState }`. **12 demos registered**: 1,2,3,4,7,8,9,10,11,12,13,14. Binding is by `data-demo` on the frame, NOT by step index.

The three-method contract:
- `init(stage)` — **idempotent hard reset to frame zero.** Called before every loop iteration. Pure DOM writes (`textContent`, `classList.remove`, `style.display`).
- `scene(e, stage)` — the async timeline. Receives the engine.
- `staticState(stage)` — reduced-motion end-state (calls `init()` then jumps to the final look).

Canonical scene tail (reset-with-fade), from slide 1 (`:3113-3120`):
```js
    await e.move(700, 460, 800);
    await e.sleep(2400);
    stage.classList.add('is-resetting');
    await e.sleep(420);
    init(stage);
    stage.classList.remove('is-resetting');
    await e.sleep(200);
```
backed by (`:170-171`):
```css
.demo-stage .wd-fade { transition: opacity 360ms ease; }
.demo-stage.is-resetting .wd-fade { opacity: 0; }
```
i.e. **elements marked `.wd-fade` fade out, state is reset invisibly, then fade back in** — this is how the loop hides the snap-back. Any region that visibly changes must be tagged `.wd-fade`.

Representative interaction idiom (`:3050-3067`) — locate, move, click, mutate, wait:
```js
