Note scenes use `document.getElementById` (`const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id)`) — **global IDs, not stage-scoped** — even though `e.q`/`e.qa` exist. That means IDs must be globally unique across all 16 slides; it's why every class/id is slide-namespaced (`s1-`, `s2-`, `s9-`…). A reuse hazard if you instantiate the same demo twice on one page.

List reordering is done by **absolute-positioned rows + a slot index → translateY**, so rows glide instead of jumping (`:2980-2984`, `:2736-2741`):
```js
  const ROW_H = 70;
  function slotRows(stage) {
    stage.querySelectorAll('.s1-row').forEach((r) => {
      r.style.transform = 'translateY(' + (parseInt(r.dataset.slot, 10) * ROW_H + 4) + 'px)';
    });
