```
Two hand-built "kits" (the only cross-slide component libraries):
- **`.wd-*` DARK INBOX KIT** — "verbatim values from conversations.css". Rebuilds WhatsApp chrome: `.wd-root .wd-avatar(.a40/.a49) .wd-icon-btn .wd-chip .wd-badge .wd-pop .wd-pop-item .wd-day .wd-wrap(.is-in/.is-out) .wd-bubble .wd-bubble-text .wd-meta .wd-composer-pill .wd-pill-btn .wd-input .wd-caret .wd-send-btn .wd-cursor .wd-ripple .wd-fade`.
- **`.lt-*` LIGHT PAGE KIT** — the main app surface: `.lt-root .lt-title .lt-serif .lt-card .lt-mid .lt-muted .lt-btn-ink .lt-btn-line .lt-pill(.p-green/.p-orange/.p-rose/.p-blue) .lt-label .lt-input`.

Everything else is **per-slide throwaway CSS** namespaced `s1-`…`s14-`, `gh-`, appended in blocks (`/* ---- slide 9 ---- */`), plus heavy inline `style=""` on structural divs. Icons are **hand-inlined SVG paths** (Lucide-shaped), including the WhatsApp glyph and three tick states stored as string constants (`TICK_CLOCK`, `TICK_ONE`, `TICK_TWO` at `:2972-2974`) swapped via `innerHTML` to animate delivery receipts.

One notable defensive detail (`:223-225`):
```css
/* Match the app's global in-shell button reset (conversations.css): strip OS chrome
   only as a FLOOR — :where() keeps specificity 0 so component classes still win. */
:where(.demo-stage button) { background: transparent; border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: inherit; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
```
State is expressed exclusively through a **stable `is-*` class vocabulary** that the CSS transitions hang off: `is-active is-open is-shown is-hover is-hidden is-unread is-on is-focus is-ready is-down is-resetting is-left is-wide is-grab is-picked is-read is-disabled is-frozen is-pulse is-check`. **This is the real abstraction** — scenes never write transforms/opacity for UI state, only classes; JS owns *when*, CSS owns *how*.

## 7. SLIDE/CHAPTER SEQUENCING (the wrapper, likely NOT reusable for marketing)

`SLIDE_META` (`:2759-2776`) drives header/segments/footer; 16 entries; `headless: true` marks text-only chapter dividers. Panes are `<section class="step-pane" data-step="N">`; the last is authored as `data-step="LAST"` and resolved at boot: `last.dataset.step = String(SLIDE_META.length - 1)`.

`render()` (`:2835-2864`) toggles `is-active`/`is-left`, updates segments/title/desc/count, then calls `startDemo(step)`. Slide transition is pure CSS (`:106-116`):
```css
.step-pane {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  padding: 24px 28px;
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(330px, 5fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
  gap: 34px; align-items: center;
  opacity: 0; transform: translateX(28px); pointer-events: none;
  transition: opacity 360ms cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1), transform 360ms cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1);
}
.step-pane.is-active { opacity: 1; transform: none; pointer-events: auto; }
.step-pane.is-left { transform: translateX(-28px); }
```
Navigation: Next/Back buttons, `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` keydown, and `#s=N` deep-link. **A hard-won bug fix worth preserving** (`:2858-2862`):
```js
    // Deep-link hash for standalone review only. In the app the deck runs inside
    // an <iframe srcdoc> (URL about:srcdoc), where replaceState to a same-origin
    // URL throws SecurityError — which would abort render() BEFORE startDemo and
    // freeze every animation. Guard it so the demos always start.
    try { history.replaceState(null, '', '#s=' + step); } catch (_) { /* srcdoc: no same-origin history */ }
```
Boot order matters: `setTimeout(render, 0)` defers first render past the synchronous `DEMOS` registrations further down the file (`:2904-2905`).

## 8. EMBEDDING / REACT LAYER

- `src/components/announcements/activeAnnouncement.tsx` — config only, 19 lines. `ACTIVE_ANNOUNCEMENT = { id: 'whats-new-whatsapp-orders-2026-07', active: true }`. Bump `id` to re-show once per user; `active:false`/`null` retires it.
- `src/components/announcements/AnnouncementGate.tsx` — reads one-shot `sessionStorage` flag `igf_pending_announcement` (armed by `src/pages/Auth.tsx` on login), mounted in `src/components/auth/ProtectedRoute.tsx`, shows deck once per login, clears flag on acknowledge.
- `src/components/announcements/AnnouncementDeck.tsx` — `fetch('/announcement-deck.html')` then renders it in a **transparent `<iframe srcDoc={html}>`**, deliberately NOT `src`: the site sends `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, which would block a network-loaded frame; `srcdoc` is inline so DENY stays in force. Two-way `postMessage` contract: deck posts `igf-announcement-ready` on boot (cancels an 8s failsafe auto-dismiss) and `igf-announcement-done` on finish/skip. `<AuthBackground/>` renders behind the transparent iframe.

Deck side of that contract (`:2874-2880`, `:2909-2911`):
```js
  function finish() {
    if (window.parent && window.parent !== window) {
      try { window.parent.postMessage({ type: 'igf-announcement-done' }, '*'); } catch (_) { /* ignore */ }
      return;
    }
    if (step !== N - 1) { step = N - 1; render(); }
  }
```
```js
  if (window.parent && window.parent !== window) {
    setTimeout(() => { try { window.parent.postMessage({ type: 'igf-announcement-ready' }, '*'); } catch (_) { /* ignore */ } }, 0);
